{# Cloudflare Turnstile widget for plain POST forms (login, registration).

   Put it INSIDE the <form>: api.js injects the hidden `cf-turnstile-response`
   field into the form containing it on its own, so the POST already carries
   the token with nothing else added. (The public /redactar flow cannot use
   this partial: it submits over fetch and keeps its own hidden input.)

   With an empty `site_key` nothing is rendered — the same switch that turns
   server-side verification off when TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is empty
   (TurnstileVerifier::isConfigured()).

   Params:
     site_key — TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY; empty = disabled
     action   — optional label Cloudflare groups its analytics by #}
{% if site_key|default('') %}
    <div class="flex justify-center">
        <div class="cf-turnstile"
             data-sitekey="{{ site_key }}"
             {% if action|default('') %}data-action="{{ action }}"{% endif %}
             data-language="es"></div>
    </div>
    <script src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>
{% endif %}
